# Passable monsters (the Chaos pets): a monster type with <flag passable="1" /> blocks no creature. Players walk
# through it (Player::canWalkthrough, and canWalkthroughEx so the creature packets mark it passable and the client
# pre-walks through it); monsters and NPCs may step onto its tile (Tile::queryAdd), path through it at no extra cost
# (AStar tile cost, monster random/dance steps) and a monster that pushes creatures never pushes or crushes it. The
# passable creature itself still needs a free tile to move to. Creature::isPassable() (false) / Monster::isPassable().
# data/monster/monsters/chaos/pets/*.xml set the flag; pets.lua has no anti-block logic any more.
# Apply in the server source root after 0001-0004: patch -p1 < 0005-passable-pets.patch, then rebuild.
